00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:31.740
Yes.

257
00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:32.380
Perfectly.

258
00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.980
I can't drink coffee out of it.

259
00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.040
Because it will fall apart from the heat.

260
00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.120
But now it's like a souvenir for you of your time in the office.

261
00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:39.960
And I love it.

262
00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:44.200
However, I did find a woman online who makes homemade pottery.

263
00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.060
She makes the Pam mug.

264
00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.780
I bought one from her.

265
00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:48.740
She didn't know it was me.

266
00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:49.720
I love it.

267
00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.100
I post about it all the time.

268
00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.000
It's made by Linda Renee Pottery.

269
00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.780
I will link to her in our stories.

270
00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.980
And you can find that in the now highlights.

271
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.840
Jenna looked at me very pointedly.

272
00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.440
And Angela, you will put it in.

273
00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.280
Will you highlight that?

274
00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.400
Yes, I will highlight it.

275
00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:07.880
I will put it in stories.

276
00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:13.260
Well, since we're on the subject of mugs, I want to plug a few of our office ladies' merch mugs, Angela.

277
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.440
They make great holiday gifts.

278
00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.880
And I don't know if everybody out there is already thinking holidays.

279
00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:23.020
But I have a personal goal to get all of my holiday shopping done by December 15th.

280
00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.720
I want to be ahead this year, not behind.

281
00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.860
No end of the year scramble for gifts.

282
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:29.320
No.

283
00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:29.660
Okay.

284
00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.960
So anyway, we have a really adorable It Is Your Mug mug.

285
00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.120
It's blue.

286
00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.660
It's so cute.

287
00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.160
The writing is etched.

288
00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.240
It's not printed on.

289
00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:39.880
It's etched.

290
00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.320
And it's that sort of light blue.

291
00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.880
And then the rim of it has like a little kind of brown ceramic color.

292
00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.880
I want you guys to know we gave Steve Carell one of these when he came into studio.

293
00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.180
And he was like, this is a good mug.

294
00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.440
It is a good mug.

295
00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:52.900
Yeah.

296
00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.040
I love the shape.

297
00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:55.280
I love the size.

298
00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:55.940
I love it.

299
00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:56.740
I love it all.

300
00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:57.580
I'm holding it in my hand.

301
00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.180
That's what she said.

302
00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.500
She said all that.

303
00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:00.980
She did.

304
00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.320
It's $35.

305
00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:07.560
We also have our Icons mug, which has little office-related images on it.

306
00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:11.060
There's a little teapot and a little yogurt lid metal and spilled chili.

307
00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.520
That one's so cute.

308
00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.180
I love it.

309
00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:13.900
It's $15.

310
00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.660
And since we are talking about the holidays, early announcement, we are bringing back all

311
00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.080
of our ugly Christmas sweatshirts.

312
00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.540
They're really cozy, including the Party Planning Committee one.

313
00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.420
And we have other holiday stuff.

314
00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:29.460
We will post a link to all of our merch and our stories.

315
00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.240
Well done, lady.

316
00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:31.820
Thank you.

317
00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.640
And finally, Angela's journal.

318
00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.720
Lady, we got a lot of mail, a lot of requests.

319
00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:42.820
Melina from Idaho said, when is Angela going to read from her journals again?

320
00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.500
It always makes me laugh out loud.

321
00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.300
Oh, my gosh.

322
00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.920
So, Ange, I wrote you.

323
00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.100
I said, can you read from your journal today?

324
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.020
Yes, I can.

325
00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:50.820
I can.

326
00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.420
And guess what?

327
00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.960
I have some Angela journal updates for everyone.

328
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.260
What are they?

329
00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.480
You know, we've been doing some home construction.

330
00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.620
And I haven't been able to get into our shed, where we keep everything, right?

331
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.880
Finally got into the shed the other day.

332
00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:06.620
We're digging around.

333
00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.380
All I was looking for was some seasonal doormats that I kept.

334
00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.240
I found a little box that said, Angela's trailer.

335
00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.920
Jenna, I didn't even find this when we were writing our book.

336
00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.640
It had a blanket in it, a pillow.

337
00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:24.420
It had, like, some extra socks.

338
00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:28.040
Like, who knows how long this little box has been in the way back of the shed.

339
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.340
But it had a journal that I kept in my trailer.

340
00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:36.320
And I wrote in it in the pilot, season one, and season two.

341
00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.260
Oh, my gosh, Angela.

342
00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:38.740
I know.

343
00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:39.780
This is such a find.

344
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.700
It's such a find.

345
00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:43.140
I wrote about the basketball episode, lady.

346
00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.020
You did not.

347
00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.460
Like, all of these specific things.

348
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.960
I was, like, in journal overload.

349
00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.540
I was like, oh, my God, what am I going to share all this?

350
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:49.940
This is all.

351
00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:51.820
But I'm going to wait.

352
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.660
I'm going to save those for special things.

353
00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.300
I wrote about filming the pilot.

354
00:14:55.840 --> 00:15:00.000
I have little notes that, like, Oscar gave me taped inside the journal.

355
00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.460
I have my call sheet, lady.

356
00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:03.500
Wow.

357
00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:04.480
I know.

358
00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.220
And we found so much stuff when we did our book.

359
00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:13.100
Is it making you want to call the publisher and say, we need to do a reprint?

360
00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:13.560
No.

361
00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.160
So I'm not going to read from that journal today.

362
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.080
I thought I would save that journal for when we get to the end of the run.

363
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.320
That's fun.

364
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:22.760
Yeah.

365
00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:23.320
Okay.

366
00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.880
Because I also found a card you gave me.

367
00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:26.440
Oh.

368
00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.040
I know.

369
00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.540
So I'm going to save all that.

370
00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:34.500
But today's Angela's Journal, you guys, I have a journal that I titled Travel Journal.

371
00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.480
Oh, it's a travel journal.

372
00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.760
And I only wrote on it when I was on a plane or a bus or a train.

373
00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:45.640
And I guess, guys, I really take inventory of who sits around me.

374
00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.100
You do, Ange.

375
00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:51.560
When you travel, you leave me the most amazing messages about the people you were surrounded

376
00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:51.880
by.

377
00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.940
It's so entertaining and detailed.

378
00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:54.460
Okay.

379
00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.920
Well, here we go, you guys.

380
00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.840
This is written at 5.56 p.m.

381
00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.360
on a flight from Philadelphia to Los Angeles.

382
00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.320
It was 2005.

383
00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:05.320
Okay.

384
00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:05.900
Okay.

385
00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.040
I have now been on this flight for three hours.

386
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.280
I write, 5.56 p.m.

387
00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.400
in all caps, BORED!

388
00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:15.900
Exclamation point.

389
00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.880
And then I write, Ken Kuapis, the director of the office, actually has a movie on this

390
00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:22.240
plane.

391
00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.440
It's the Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants.

392
00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:26.120
It was the feature movie.

393
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.920
I saw it with Jenna at the theater when it came out, so I didn't feel like paying $5

394
00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.260
for headphones.

395
00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:33.640
Frowny face.

396
00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:34.920
Oh, yeah.

397
00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.780
Now they give you headphones.

398
00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:37.360
Yeah.

399
00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.100
This is in 2005.

400
00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:44.300
I go on to say, and now the odd couple is on, and I wish I had a pair of headphones.

401
00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:49.100
The guy behind me is pounding Jack Daniels and Coke.

402
00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:51.160
I think he's finally passed out.

403
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.020
Oh, and the two ladies in front of me are feuding.

404
00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:58.820
One wanted the other to switch so her husband could sit next to her, but the other lady said

405
00:16:58.820 --> 00:16:59.160
no.

406
00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.580
She didn't want to give up her seat.

407
00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.600
It's been tense ever since.

408
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.080
This is amazing.

409
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.040
This part cracks me up.

410
00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:11.800
The guy next to me has been diligently reading a book on Texas Hold'em and furiously scribbling

411
00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:12.140
notes.

412
00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.780
He ran out of paper and has started to write on his plane ticket.

413
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.600
He keeps covering his notes with his hand, like I'm going to steal his secrets.

414
00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.620
I'd offer him a page out of this journal, but he's such a grump.

415
00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.060
We should be landing in half an hour, and I'm starving, and there's no snacks on U.S.

416
00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:30.540
Airways

417
00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:32.180
unless you want to pay $7.

418
00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:33.580
Ridiculous.

419
00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.100
What happened to the airline industry?

420
00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.580
Question mark, exclamation point.

421
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.360
It was amazing, Angela.

422
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.560
Oh, you guys.

423
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.700
I loved it.

424
00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.840
I loved it.

425
00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.460
Can you believe I wouldn't give the guy a piece of paper?

426
00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.400
He's like writing on his plane ticket.

427
00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:57.820
You're not going to give the airline $5 for headphones or $7 for a snack.

428
00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.220
You're not sharing your paper.

429
00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:02.540
I'm not going to spend $12 on things I need.

430
00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:03.240
No.

431
00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.360
Oh, ridiculous.

432
00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.560
$7 for snacks.

433
00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.880
I absolutely loved it.

434
00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.180
Well, there you go.

435
00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.940
That's my Angela's Journals updates.

436
00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:20.740
I will save some of our early years that I wrote about for the end of our run.

437
00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.980
That's all I got for Fast Facts, lady.

438
00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:27.100
I could really just do a whole episode of you reading your journals.

439
00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:31.580
You know what this made me want to do is journal again when I travel.

440
00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.320
Because I used to always journal.

441
00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:34.260
Me too.

442
00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:35.200
Yeah.

443
00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.120
It's such good character study.

444
00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:40.800
If you're a writer or an actor, it's great character study.

445
00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:45.520
I always love your messages when you've gotten off a plane because that's what they are.

446
00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.340
That's the description I get.

447
00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.420
You really paint a picture.

448
00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.140
All right.

449
00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.140
Well, should we take a break?

450
00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.160
And then when we come back, does Stanley have a mustache?

451
00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:56.040
Oh, there's a hot debate.

452
00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:11.310
Well, the episode's going to start with Pam and Phyllis.

453
00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:16.610
They're passing around a card for everyone to sign, welcoming Stanley back from his tonsil

454
00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.050
surgery.

455
00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:23.970
I guess the card says, quote, glad they didn't mix up your tonsillectomy with a mustacheectomy.

456
00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.330
We get some gym sass.

457
00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.490
He says, oh, that's not good.

458
00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.130
Met with some Phyllis sass.

459
00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.490
She's like, oh, because your jokes are all hilarious.

460
00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:34.150
You know what, lady?

461
00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.710
This made me realize we really like a punny card on this show.

462
00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:38.630
Mm-hmm.

463
00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:42.490
Remember in the Alliance, Meredith got a card that said, happy bird day?

464
00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:43.010
Yep.

465
00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.230
Do you have a memory of getting a real pun card?

466
00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:46.890
Because I do.

467
00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.770
No, we give my dad pun cards.

468
00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.150
Does he like a pun card?

469
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.270
He loves a pun.

470
00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.570
He's a punner.

471
00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:54.870
There's one in every family.

472
00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:55.270
Mm-hmm.

473
00:19:55.750 --> 00:20:00.170
I am not the punner, but somehow I still get cards with puns.

474
00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:05.970
I got one one time from a friend of mine that it was just a picture of a sofa, and it said,

475
00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.690
you're Sofa King Awesome.

476
00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.050
It took me a second.

477
00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:14.530
Clever.

478
00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:19.370
Well, Jim is going to question whether or not Stanley has a mustache.

479
00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:19.970
Yeah.

480
00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:24.330
And everyone's like, no, he does have a mustache.

481
00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.270
Well, some people feel very strongly that he does.

482
00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.530
Some people feel like, no way, he does not.

483
00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.970
And then some people are waffling.

484
00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.610
I did break it down.

485
00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.250
Here's how the Dunder Mifflin Bunch voted by show of hands.

486
00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.630
Team Stash are Pam, Dwight, Creed, and Oscar.

487
00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.150
Team No Stash, Jim, Phyllis, Angela.

488
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.090
Team Unsure About the Stash, Kevin.

489
00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.670
I feel like Phyllis raises both hands.

490
00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.970
She has two hands up at the end.

491
00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:50.970
Yes, that's true.

492
00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.450
She might be unsure.

493
00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.410
She might be in Team Unsure Stash.

494
00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.310
I mean, Pam even draws a picture.

495
00:20:56.310 --> 00:21:00.430
She draws a mustache Stanley and a no mustache Stanley.

496
00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:02.210
That didn't seem to help.

497
00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:05.050
But we did get a lot of mail about these drawings.

498
00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:05.990
Jocelyn V.

499
00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.130
in St. George, Utah, Millie P.

500
00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.330
from Durham, North Carolina, and Zoe G.

501
00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:11.790
from Irvine, California,

502
00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:17.910
all said, Jenna, in the cold open when everyone is trying to remember whether or not Stanley has a mustache,

503
00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.030
Pam draws two pictures of Stanley in eight seconds.

504
00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.190
That's very funny.

505
00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:32.690
At 50 seconds, she is standing next to Phyllis, and at 58, she says okay and then holds up two full-page recognizable sketches of Stanley.

506
00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:40.290
In re-watching the scene, Pam's frantic faux-speed sketching in the background of Jim's line had me cracking up.

507
00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.690
That means she only had four seconds for each of those pictures.

508
00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.070
Who really drew those pictures?

509
00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:48.790
Were you directed to draw really fast?

510
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:52.050
Please tell us everything you remember about this scene.

511
00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.410
Well, Jocelyn, Millie, and Zoe, I have a curveball to throw at you.

512
00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:01.830
What if Pam has sketched everyone in the office and keeps them in her desk drawer?

513
00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.350
That sounds like something Dwight would do.

514
00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:05.670
I know.

515
00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.510
Because he's going to need a wanted poster at any moment.

